course: dictionary
lesson: 8193
title: Restorative: making things right
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Restorative has three: something that makes you feel well and calm again, a way of dealing with wrongdoing in schools and courts, and an old word for a drink or medicine that gives you strength back. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Restorative justice brings the wrongdoer and the person harmed together to put things right.» The clues are wrongdoer, harmed and put things right. This is about mending a problem between people, not about feeling better in your body.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence: "Restorative justice brings them together to put things right" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Restore means to bring something back to how it was, and restorative means it helps that happen.
fact: Restorative means helping to make something healthy, strong, calm or right again.
fact: «A restorative sleep» is a sleep that leaves you feeling strong and calm again.
fact: Restorative justice is a way of dealing with wrongdoing where both sides talk, and it aims to mend the relationship rather than only punish.
fact: «A restorative meeting» is a talk where people who fell out say what happened and how to put it right.
fact: As a noun, a restorative is an old word for a drink or medicine that gives you strength back.
exercise: «Restorative justice brings the wrongdoer and the person harmed together to put things right.» What does restorative justice aim to do? | Only punish the wrongdoer harshly | Close the school for the day | Make everyone forget what happened | *Bring people together to put things right
exercise: «After a long walk, a cup of tea was restorative.» What does restorative mean here? | Sent away to another school | Very cold and wet | Noisy and busy | *Making you feel calm and strong again
exercise: «A restorative meeting is a talk where people who fell out say what happened and how to put it right.» Find and copy the word that means someone who does harm. | *wrongdoer | restorative | together | justice
test: «He had a restorative sleep and woke up feeling strong again.» What does restorative mean here? | *Making him feel healthy and calm again | Sad and lonely | Short and noisy | Very dark
test: In many schools, what do restorative conversations replace? | Homework | *Plain punishment after a fight | Spelling tests | Lunch breaks
exam: Which best describes restorative justice? | Giving a prize to the winner | *Bringing both sides together to talk and put things right | Only punishing the person who did wrong | Ignoring what happened
